Becky White (Edited)
Interviewee: White, Becky

But in a way we suffered, I guess, I don't want to say abuse, but we bore the brunt of my parents' inability to relate and connect with each other. And then the trauma that my mom carried her whole life. So, those were actually big factors for why I eventually came to Korea. To learn more about my mom and myself, learn Korean language so that I could better understand (chuckles) what happened. (laughs) I was extremely independent, this is important to remember. So, I didn't strongly relate to anything. I didn't really strongly relate to myself as American or white or Korean. I was just so firmly me, that I could flit in and out of anything I wanted to;
